IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P9-gate`

-- P9-art-112: Article 112 "Evaluation and review" (consolidated text of 27.7.2026; not changed by the Omnibus). Group General (2 August 2026).
-- The Commission, the AI Office, the Board, the Member States and the national competent authorities are officials: no seat.
-- What Article 112 means to a seat: paragraph 12 (the specificities of the sector of Section B of Annex I) for a product manufacturer.
-- Every function takes `the date asked` first; before the group applies the answer is NOTHING, and a regulative rule owes nothing (FULFILLED).
-- A report due "by [a date] and every four years thereafter" is the n-th report, n counted from 1 (the caller states n); the deadline of
-- the n-th report is the first date plus four (or three) years for each earlier one. A rule with a date has a breach path; a duty with no
-- date ("shall provide ... without undue delay", "shall take into account") has none, and is listed in NOTES.md.
-- The time is counted from a day the caller states (the day the duty began), as in Articles 81, 91, 92 and 96.

§ `Article 112: the parties and the acts`

DECLARE `Art 112 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 112 the Commission`
    `Art 112 the AI Office`
    `Art 112 the Board, a Member State or a national competent authority`

DECLARE `Art 112 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 112(1) assess the need for amendment of the list set out in Annex III and of the list of prohibited AI practices laid down in Article 5`
    `Art 112(1) submit the findings of that assessment to the European Parliament and the Council`
    `Art 112(2) evaluate and report to the European Parliament and to the Council on the matters of paragraph 2`
    `Art 112(3) submit a report on the evaluation and review of this Regulation to the European Parliament and to the Council`
    `Art 112(5) evaluate the functioning of the AI Office and submit a report to the European Parliament and to the Council`
    `Art 112(6) submit a report on the review of the progress on the development of standardisation deliverables on the energy-efficient development of general-purpose AI models`
    `Art 112(7) evaluate the impact and effectiveness of voluntary codes of conduct`
    `Art 112(8) provide the Commission with information upon its request and without undue delay`
    `Art 112(9) take into account the positions and findings of the Board, of the European Parliament, of the Council, and of other relevant bodies or sources`
    `Art 112(10) submit appropriate proposals to amend this Regulation`
    `Art 112(11) undertake to develop an objective and participative methodology for the evaluation of risk levels`
    `Art 112(12) take into account the regulatory specificities of each sector and the existing governance, conformity assessment and enforcement mechanisms and authorities`
    `Art 112(13) carry out an assessment of the enforcement of this Regulation and report on it to the European Parliament, the Council and the European Economic and Social Committee`

§ `Article 112(1): the yearly assessment`

-- "once a year following the entry into force of this Regulation, and until the end of the period of the delegation of power laid down in Article 97".
-- The n-th assessment is due by the n-th anniversary of the entry into force (a reading: fork F-112-1).
-- src:1631 | 1. The Commission shall assess the need for amendment of the list set out in Annex III and of the list of prohibited AI practices laid down in Article 5, once a year following the entry into force of this Regulation, and until the end of the period of the delegation of power laid down in Article 97. The Commission shall submit the findings of that assessment to the European Parliament and the Council.
@ref Art 112(1) (src:1631)
GIVEN `the number of the year following the entry into force` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`Art 112(1) the day by which the assessment for the year must be made` MEANS
    `add years` `Art 113 the Regulation enters into force` `the number of the year following the entry into force`

@ref Art 112(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the period of the delegation of power laid down in Article 97 has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 112(1) the Commission must assess the need for amendment of the lists in Annex III and Article 5` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF `the period of the delegation of power laid down in Article 97 has ended`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "once a year following the entry into force of this Regulation, and until the end of the period of the delegation of power laid down in Article 97" (an "until" bar that has been reached)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref Art 112(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the period of the delegation of power laid down in Article 97 has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of the year following the entry into force` IS A NUMBER
      `the day from which the time is counted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 112 party` `Art 112 act`
`Art 112(1) the duty of the Commission to assess the need for amendment once a year` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: Article 113 gives this provision its date of application
    ELSE IF `the period of the delegation of power laid down in Article 97 has ended` OR `the number of the year following the entry into force` AT MOST 0
         THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the assessment is "until the end of the period of the delegation of power laid down in Article 97"
         ELSE PARTY `Art 112 the Commission`
              MUST `Art 112(1) assess the need for amendment of the list set out in Annex III and of the list of prohibited AI practices laid down in Article 5`
              WITHIN (Day (`Art 112(1) the day by which the assessment for the year must be made` `the number of the year following the entry into force`)) MINUS (Day `the day from which the time is counted`)
              HENCE FULFILLED
              LEST BREACH BY `Art 112 the Commission` BECAUSE "the need for amendment of the list set out in Annex III and of the list of prohibited AI practices laid down in Article 5 was not assessed within the year"

@ref Art 112(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission has assessed the need for amendment of the lists in Annex III and Article 5` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 112(1) the Commission must submit the findings of that assessment to the European Parliament and the Council` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF `the Commission has assessed the need for amendment of the lists in Annex III and Article 5`
         THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text sets no date for the submission
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is to submit "the findings of that assessment", which exist once the assessment is made

@ref Art 112(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission has assessed the need for amendment of the lists in Annex III and Article 5` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 112 party` `Art 112 act`
`Art 112(1) the duty of the Commission to submit the findings of the assessment to the European Parliament and the Council` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 112(1) the Commission must submit the findings of that assessment to the European Parliament and the Council` `the date asked` `the Commission has assessed the need for amendment of the lists in Annex III and Article 5`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY `Art 112 the Commission`
        MUST `Art 112(1) submit the findings of that assessment to the European Parliament and the Council`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

§ `Article 112(2): the report every four years from 2 August 2028`

-- src:1632 | 2. By 2 August 2028 and every four years thereafter, the Commission shall evaluate and report to the European Parliament and to the Council on the following:
-- src:1633 | (a) the need for amendments extending existing area headings or adding new area headings in Annex III;
-- src:1634 | (b) amendments to the list of AI systems requiring additional transparency measures in Article 50;
-- src:1635 | (c) amendments enhancing the effectiveness of the supervision and governance system.
@ref Art 112(2) (src:1632-1635)
GIVEN `the number of the report` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`Art 112(2) the day by which the Commission must evaluate and report` MEANS
    `add years` (Date 2 8 2028) (4 TIMES (`the number of the report` MINUS 1))  -- "By 2 August 2028 and every four years thereafter"

@ref Art 112(2)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the number of the report` IS A NUMBER
      `the day from which the time is counted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 112 party` `Art 112 act`
`Art 112(2) the duty of the Commission to evaluate and report` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)) OR `the number of the report` AT MOST 0
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: Article 113 gives this provision its date of application
    ELSE PARTY `Art 112 the Commission`
         MUST `Art 112(2) evaluate and report to the European Parliament and to the Council on the matters of paragraph 2`
         WITHIN (Day (`Art 112(2) the day by which the Commission must evaluate and report` `the number of the report`)) MINUS (Day `the day from which the time is counted`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `Art 112 the Commission` BECAUSE "the Commission did not evaluate and report to the European Parliament and to the Council by 2 August 2028 and every four years thereafter"

DECLARE `Art 112(2) matter` IS ONE OF
    `Art 112(2)(a) the need for amendments extending existing area headings or adding new area headings in Annex III`
    `Art 112(2)(b) amendments to the list of AI systems requiring additional transparency measures in Article 50`
    `Art 112(2)(c) amendments enhancing the effectiveness of the supervision and governance system`
    `Art 112(2) another matter`

@ref Art 112(2)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the matter` IS AN `Art 112(2) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 112(2) the Commission must evaluate and report on the matter` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE CONSIDER `the matter`
         WHEN `Art 112(2) another matter` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "on the following" names points (a) to (c) and the list is not closed by "only"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Art 112(4) point` IS ONE OF
    `Art 112(4)(a) the status of the financial, technical and human resources of the national competent authorities`
    `Art 112(4)(b) the state of penalties, in particular administrative fines as referred to in Article 99(1), applied by Member States for infringements of this Regulation`
    `Art 112(4)(c) adopted harmonised standards and common specifications developed to support this Regulation`
    `Art 112(4)(d) the number of undertakings that enter the market after the entry into application of this Regulation, and how many of them are SMEs`
    `Art 112(4) another point`

-- src:1637 | 4. The reports referred to in paragraph 2 shall pay specific attention to the following:
-- src:1638 | (a) the status of the financial, technical and human resources of the national competent authorities in order to effectively perform the tasks assigned to them under this Regulation;
-- src:1639 | (b) the state of penalties, in particular administrative fines as referred to in Article 99(1), applied by Member States for infringements of this Regulation;
-- src:1640 | (c) adopted harmonised standards and common specifications developed to support this Regulation;
-- src:1641 | (d) the number of undertakings that enter the market after the entry into application of this Regulation, and how many of them are SMEs.
@ref Art 112(4) (src:1637-1641)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the point` IS AN `Art 112(4) point`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 112(4) the reports referred to in paragraph 2 must pay specific attention to the point` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE CONSIDER `the point`
         WHEN `Art 112(4) another point` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "shall pay specific attention to the following" names points (a) to (d) and does not say "only"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Article 112(3): the report every four years from 2 August 2029`

-- src:1636 | 3. By 2 August 2029 and every four years thereafter, the Commission shall submit a report on the evaluation and review of this Regulation to the European Parliament and to the Council. The report shall include an assessment with regard to the structure of enforcement and the possible need for a Union agency to resolve any identified shortcomings. On the basis of the findings, that report shall, where appropriate, be accompanied by a proposal for amendment of this Regulation. The reports shall be made public.
@ref Art 112(3) (src:1636)
GIVEN `the number of the report` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`Art 112(3) the day by which the Commission must submit the report` MEANS
    `add years` (Date 2 8 2029) (4 TIMES (`the number of the report` MINUS 1))  -- "By 2 August 2029 and every four years thereafter"

@ref Art 112(3)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the number of the report` IS A NUMBER
      `the day from which the time is counted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 112 party` `Art 112 act`
`Art 112(3) the duty of the Commission to submit the report on the evaluation and review of this Regulation` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)) OR `the number of the report` AT MOST 0
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: Article 113 gives this provision its date of application
    ELSE PARTY `Art 112 the Commission`
         MUST `Art 112(3) submit a report on the evaluation and review of this Regulation to the European Parliament and to the Council`
         WITHIN (Day (`Art 112(3) the day by which the Commission must submit the report` `the number of the report`)) MINUS (Day `the day from which the time is counted`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `Art 112 the Commission` BECAUSE "the Commission did not submit the report on the evaluation and review of this Regulation by 2 August 2029 and every four years thereafter"

@ref Art 112(3)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the report has been submitted under Article 112(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 112(3) the reports must be made public` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF `the report has been submitted under Article 112(3)`
         THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text sets no date by which the report is made public
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "the reports", the reports of this paragraph

@ref Art 112(3)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the report has been submitted under Article 112(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 112 party` `Art 112 act`
`Art 112(3) the duty of the Commission to make the reports public` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 112(3) the reports must be made public` `the date asked` `the report has been submitted under Article 112(3)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY `Art 112 the Commission`
        MUST `Art 112(3) submit a report on the evaluation and review of this Regulation to the European Parliament and to the Council`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

@ref Art 112(3)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the findings are available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate to accompany the report with a proposal for amendment of this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 112(3) the report must be accompanied by a proposal for amendment of this Regulation` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF NOT `the findings are available`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On the basis of the findings, that report shall, where appropriate, be accompanied by a proposal"
         ELSE IF `it is appropriate to accompany the report with a proposal for amendment of this Regulation`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that report shall, where appropriate, be accompanied by a proposal for amendment of this Regulation" (a "where appropriate" gate on a duty that is not met: fork F-112-3)

§ `Article 112(5), (6), (7): the other evaluations and reports`

